WEBVTT

00:00:03.187 --> 00:00:06.566
A voice media clip travels as its library entry:

00:00:06.566 --> 00:00:09.507
its name, its description and its format.

00:00:09.507 --> 00:00:12.447
The audio file itself is not in the plan.

00:00:12.447 --> 00:00:17.453
Here the clip was deleted before the import, and it came back as an entry.

00:00:17.453 --> 00:00:21.707
Its badges still say Master copy, but the audio is not at this

00:00:21.707 --> 00:00:23.897
site, so you upload it again.

00:00:24.351 --> 00:00:27.238
Open the clip and choose the audio file again.

00:00:27.238 --> 00:00:31.902
Because the clip keeps its identifier, the queues, entry points and menus that

00:00:31.902 --> 00:00:33.901
use it start playing it again.

00:00:34.355 --> 00:00:35.053
Save.

00:00:35.053 --> 00:00:40.127
The platform keeps the master copy and sends a copy to the phone provider.

00:00:40.127 --> 00:00:45.011
Here the provider is unreachable, so it warns that the provider did not

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.675
accept the copy, and sends it later.

